.TH @BINUP@ 1 "@DATE@" "@NAME@ @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@BIN@ \- @SUMMARY_EN@
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @BIN@
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @NAME@
@DESC_EN@
.PP
It is a diary for health-related data, not a medical device. Use at your own risk.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the command line help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.BI \-d " file" "\fR, \fP\-\-database " file
Open the given database file.
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Start with the demo database containing sample data.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/@BIN@/docs/
User manuals as PDF (German and English), opened with F1.
.TP
.I ~/.config/VitaParms/@SETTINGS@.conf
Settings.
.SH SEE ALSO
The user manual (Help menu or F1).
.SH AUTHOR
Michael Bergmann. Licensed under the MIT license.
